WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.049 --> 00:00:04.220
Film Courage: What is the biggest audition
you’ve ever had?

00:00:04.220 --> 00:00:12.260
Chad Lindberg: Wow…the biggest audition
I’ve ever had?

00:00:12.260 --> 00:00:20.980
Good question…I would say the OCTOBER SKY
audition I had was the biggest.

00:00:20.980 --> 00:00:25.340
You went from the casting director, then the
director, and then I got the screen test which

00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:30.659
is interesting because they put you up in
the clothes and the outfits and they actually

00:00:30.659 --> 00:00:32.419
film you doing this scene.

00:00:32.419 --> 00:00:36.399
You’ve got two other actors who are hoping
to get the same part.

00:00:36.399 --> 00:00:42.859
And they come up and they dress them up identical
to you and you get really, really close.

00:00:42.859 --> 00:00:45.719
And I ended up getting the movie and it worked.

00:00:45.719 --> 00:00:50.179
And then you think about the other two guys
who showed up on set and went through the

00:00:50.179 --> 00:00:55.540
whole rigmarole and you’ve got to sign paperwork
and everything and it doesn’t happen.

00:00:55.540 --> 00:01:00.109
So you definitely feel the stakes are pretty
high.

00:01:00.109 --> 00:01:05.810
And then an interesting audition story that
I tell a lot is…and again this is something

00:01:05.810 --> 00:01:12.410
I learned from, when the Fast and the Furious
audition came my way…again where I was at

00:01:12.410 --> 00:01:16.320
that time in my life I didn’t realize what
I had.

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:22.230
I was off in my sort of thinking about what
I thought about the business.

00:01:22.230 --> 00:01:28.950
I got the audition and it was called REDLINE
actually at the time and I remember passing

00:01:28.950 --> 00:01:29.950
on the audition.

00:01:29.950 --> 00:01:30.950
Why?

00:01:30.950 --> 00:01:36.630
Because I just did not want to…I had in
my mind I just wanted to do something completely

00:01:36.630 --> 00:01:40.950
different with my life at the time and maybe
23-years-old and [smiles to himself as he

00:01:40.950 --> 00:01:41.950
looks up].

00:01:41.950 --> 00:01:42.950
So I got the audition.

00:01:42.950 --> 00:01:43.950
I passed.

00:01:43.950 --> 00:01:45.510
I got the audition twice.

00:01:45.510 --> 00:01:46.990
I passed.

00:01:46.990 --> 00:01:47.990
Right?

00:01:47.990 --> 00:01:52.860
My agent at the time calls me up and says
“What are you doing?

00:01:52.860 --> 00:01:55.612
Do you really want to pass on this?” and
I said “Yeah!”

00:01:55.612 --> 00:01:57.040
I mean I was just being a little punk.

00:01:57.040 --> 00:02:00.310
She’s like “Fine!” and hung up the phone
on me.

00:02:00.310 --> 00:02:04.380
And I’m like “Yeah…I’m making these
decisions!”

00:02:04.380 --> 00:02:05.650
[Laughs].

00:02:05.650 --> 00:02:08.970
Another agent from the same agency calls me
up and said “Chad….you know…come on…

00:02:08.970 --> 00:02:12.861
Go in [to read again for the role]…just
go in.”

00:02:12.861 --> 00:02:14.800
And I was like “Okay!

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:16.410
I’ll go in.”

00:02:16.410 --> 00:02:18.200
I was being a brat.

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:20.440
I was being a brat!

00:02:20.440 --> 00:02:25.320
And I went in and auditioned and I met with
the director, Rob Cohen and he’s friendly

00:02:25.320 --> 00:02:26.320
and so nice.

00:02:26.320 --> 00:02:34.960
And the casting director who I love and so
I auditioned and they loved what I did and

00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:39.069
then they called me back to read with a couple
of the other actors.

00:02:39.069 --> 00:02:44.450
And then you start to play it in your mind.

00:02:44.450 --> 00:02:47.330
You’re like “Oh…you like me!

00:02:47.330 --> 00:02:48.650
Okay…Yeah…I’ll go back in.

00:02:48.650 --> 00:02:49.650
Yeah, sure.”

00:02:49.650 --> 00:02:55.870
So I go in and I read with…I think it was
Matt Schulze at the time and Johnny Tran I

00:02:55.870 --> 00:02:56.870
believe.

00:02:56.870 --> 00:02:57.870
And they were trying to fit the guys.

00:02:57.870 --> 00:03:02.690
They already had Paul [Walker] and Vin [Diesel].

00:03:02.690 --> 00:03:04.750
And I ended up booking this movie.

00:03:04.750 --> 00:03:07.740
I ended up booking this movie, I got the part
and I’m like “Wow!

00:03:07.740 --> 00:03:09.530
This is really cool.

00:03:09.530 --> 00:03:14.770
And we’re going to do all these cars”
and then I got on set and it became this crazy

00:03:14.770 --> 00:03:16.090
thing and everyone was like “It’s going
to be huge.

00:03:16.090 --> 00:03:17.090
It’s going to be this big movie.”

00:03:17.090 --> 00:03:22.080
And I’m just like “No…I just don’t
think so guys.”

00:03:22.080 --> 00:03:25.880
I was just so locked into this brain of mine.

00:03:25.880 --> 00:03:30.030
And then, low and behold it became this huge
phenomenon.

00:03:30.030 --> 00:03:32.430
It changed my life instantly.

00:03:32.430 --> 00:03:35.720
And it taught me (again) that you never, never,
never know.

00:03:35.720 --> 00:03:37.590
Don’t turn down an audition.

00:03:37.590 --> 00:03:39.020
Don’t be silly.

00:03:39.020 --> 00:03:41.520
And I was really silly.

00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:49.660
And I tell this story and I am soooo appreciative
that I went in and that I was given that opportunity

00:03:49.660 --> 00:03:52.020
and it changed my life forever.

00:03:52.020 --> 00:03:53.020
Forever!

00:03:53.020 --> 00:03:57.050
So I learned a valuable lesson then, you know.

00:03:57.050 --> 00:04:00.280
Just keep your mind open.

00:04:00.280 --> 00:04:01.280
Appreciate what you have.

00:04:01.280 --> 00:04:02.459
If it comes when you’re 19.

00:04:02.459 --> 00:04:04.980
If it comes when you’re 40.

00:04:04.980 --> 00:04:05.980
So…

00:04:05.980 --> 00:04:10.390
Film Courage: What were you hoping for at
23?

00:04:10.390 --> 00:04:15.709
What type of role would you have thought was
more….I mean I realize a lot of actors [don’t

00:04:15.709 --> 00:04:18.079
know what the film will do] and then they
see later.

00:04:18.079 --> 00:04:19.650
But what were you hoping for?

00:04:19.650 --> 00:04:24.139
Chad Lindberg: I guess at that time I wanted
to do something edgy and hardcore…

00:04:24.139 --> 00:04:27.449
Film Courage: Like a David Lynch film?

00:04:27.449 --> 00:04:28.870
Chad Lindberg: Yeah!

00:04:28.870 --> 00:04:36.629
[Thinks for a moment] You know, maybe it was
again the computer geek [role], like Computer

00:04:36.629 --> 00:04:42.100
Geek Jesse and it was in my mind I was sort
of like pushing away those characters.

00:04:42.100 --> 00:04:47.919
Because I just kept getting computer guy…computer
this…computer that and it drove me crazy!

00:04:47.919 --> 00:04:51.050
So maybe that also played a part in that and
I was sort of pushing that away.

00:04:51.050 --> 00:04:52.050
And [I’m like] No!

00:04:52.050 --> 00:04:57.830
I’m not that guy and I want to do something
crazy and swear and be a crazy, weird guy.

00:04:57.830 --> 00:05:04.360
And again, when it’s your part, it’s a
very personal thing and it will find you.

00:05:04.360 --> 00:05:05.460
It will find you.

00:05:05.460 --> 00:05:10.610
And I’m so lucky that it did because that
movie has now become [looks up in wonder]…they

00:05:10.610 --> 00:05:13.099
are working on [Fast and Furious] number eight.

00:05:13.099 --> 00:05:17.759
And it’s like people recognize me from it
every day and they tell me how much that movie

00:05:17.759 --> 00:05:19.059
means to them.

00:05:19.059 --> 00:05:20.680
How many times they have seen it.

00:05:20.680 --> 00:05:27.270
And so I’m like….[exhales] and I’ve
been very lucky.

00:05:27.270 --> 00:05:28.362
Yeah…you just never know.

00:05:28.362 --> 00:05:31.990
Film Courage: Did you ever drive you’re
own white [Volkswagen] Jetta?

00:05:31.990 --> 00:05:36.080
Chad Lindberg: [Laughs] No…and they barely
let us drive in the movie, too.

00:05:36.080 --> 00:05:39.289
Because you just don’t give actors cars
on set.

00:05:39.289 --> 00:05:44.509
We got to drive a little bit and then they
would put us in picture cars, which was great.

00:05:44.509 --> 00:05:49.220
And the scene where I am racing Johnny Tran
they had tied up my car.

00:05:49.220 --> 00:05:50.220
It was a picture car.

00:05:50.220 --> 00:05:54.289
They tied it up to a semi [truck] and they
hauled me at like 70-80 miles per hour and

00:05:54.289 --> 00:05:58.710
then they put another car racing next to me
for my eye line.

00:05:58.710 --> 00:06:02.470
So when I’m driving like this, you are actually
racing someone for real.

00:06:02.470 --> 00:06:12.330
They are obviously in control and the cameras
are on the bed of the truck.

00:06:12.330 --> 00:06:17.509
But yeah…looking back, it was so cool.

00:06:17.509 --> 00:06:24.550
I want to do something like that now and have
the greater appreciation and the majestical

00:06:24.550 --> 00:06:27.460
scope I have now about this business.

00:06:27.460 --> 00:06:34.279
I think that would be a huge thrill to kind
of go back and do something like that, but

00:06:34.279 --> 00:06:36.509
then again you just never know.

00:06:36.509 --> 00:06:41.009
The movies that you think are going to be
huge…no, not so much.

00:06:41.009 --> 00:06:43.020
The movies that you think “Oh…I don’t
know?”

00:06:43.020 --> 00:06:44.930
turn out to be phenomenal.

00:06:44.930 --> 00:06:45.930
So yeah…

00:06:45.930 --> 00:06:51.399
Film Courage: Well that’s the beauty of
being 23, you don’t sometimes realize what

00:06:51.399 --> 00:06:53.460
is being given to you.

00:06:53.460 --> 00:06:57.080
Chad Lindberg: Yeah…there’s a beauty to
that, too.

00:06:57.080 --> 00:07:00.369
I had no idea and that taught me a lot.

00:07:00.369 --> 00:07:06.559
Film Courage: Going back to OCTOBER SKY, where
were you in your life when you had that audition?

00:07:06.559 --> 00:07:07.559
What was your mindset?

00:07:07.559 --> 00:07:09.460
Chad Lindberg: I was barely 21 years old.

00:07:09.460 --> 00:07:14.599
I had turned 21 and was in sort of the same
mindset.

00:07:14.599 --> 00:07:19.690
I remember being on set and thinking “I
don’t know?”

00:07:19.690 --> 00:07:27.539
I love this interview because it makes me
reflect and it makes me go back and re-appreciate

00:07:27.539 --> 00:07:32.520
the things that I’ve gone through and been
through and that have worked out.

00:07:32.520 --> 00:07:35.300
It’s scary to think “What if it didn’t
work out?

00:07:35.300 --> 00:07:36.680
Where would I be?

00:07:36.680 --> 00:07:38.669
What would I be doing?”

00:07:38.669 --> 00:07:40.110
So I was a fresh 21.

00:07:40.110 --> 00:07:45.360
Now I am on set with all of these picture
cars.

00:07:45.360 --> 00:07:49.939
It was in this time period and we’re telling
this story about Homer Hickam and THE ROCKET

00:07:49.939 --> 00:07:56.460
BOYS and Jake Gyllenhaal was 16 at that time.

00:07:56.460 --> 00:08:00.490
He still had to do school on the set.

00:08:00.490 --> 00:08:08.960
And William Lee Scott and I were the two oldest
and the only thing to do in Tennessee was

00:08:08.960 --> 00:08:09.960
the 24-hour Walmart.

00:08:09.960 --> 00:08:10.960
Film Courage: Oh.

00:08:10.960 --> 00:08:11.960
Nice!

00:08:11.960 --> 00:08:15.199
Chad Lindberg: [Laughs] And that is how we
kept ourselves busy.

00:08:15.199 --> 00:08:21.360
And I remember the studios sending us Playstations
when we got this part.

00:08:21.360 --> 00:08:25.849
And we’re like these kids and we’re like
“You’re sending us these Playstations?”

00:08:25.849 --> 00:08:30.229
All of the sudden you are just being thrown
all of these opportunities.

00:08:30.229 --> 00:08:33.870
And again when you’re young and you don’t
realize it.

00:08:33.870 --> 00:08:36.750
But that was one of the greatest times ever.

00:08:36.750 --> 00:08:41.680
One of the most pure….when you’re that
age you’re not really thinking about all

00:08:41.680 --> 00:08:44.370
the adult stuff that has to come into play.

00:08:44.370 --> 00:08:46.600
You know that we worry about much later on.

00:08:46.600 --> 00:08:52.779
We were just free and had fun.

00:08:52.779 --> 00:09:01.000
And they just did a Rocket Boys Festival that
I attended not to long ago for its anniversary…was

00:09:01.000 --> 00:09:02.420
it 15 years ago?

00:09:02.420 --> 00:09:03.420
No wait!

00:09:03.420 --> 00:09:05.259
That was THE FAST AND THE FURIOUS.

00:09:05.259 --> 00:09:06.259
Probably longer.

00:09:06.259 --> 00:09:07.259
I don’t know.

00:09:07.259 --> 00:09:11.250
All of these anniversaries just remind me
of how much I’ve been in this industry.

00:09:11.250 --> 00:09:12.250
But yeah.

00:09:12.250 --> 00:09:14.949
It’s cool to see where all of these projects
go and what they become.

00:09:14.949 --> 00:09:15.949
Question for the Viewers: Which movie do you
wish you could audition for?

00:09:15.949 --> 00:09:16.449
What role?

